From b5ca980c299421087d4f99a01c6c01596347f3a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NickT72 <35966711+Nicktili72@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 14:59:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] daemon: inline upload bytes for Safari browsers

A Safari Web Extension is sandboxed and cannot read the staged_path the daemon
injects into tool.upload. For browsers whose handshake name is Safari the daemon
now also sends each file's bytes as UploadFile.data_base64 (standard base64,
capped at 16 MiB per call; larger uploads get an invalid_params error that says
so). The read runs on a blocking thread like the rest of upload staging. Other
browsers are unaffected. The field is daemon-injected and never agent-facing;
the upload params schema is regenerated.
---
